.uk/news/articles/cew92lp2g45o--5d7564af3869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cew92lp2g45o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC's Laura Cress gets a first look at the biggest games in Cologne from Witcher 3 to Alien: Isolation 2.</summary></entry><entry><title>Matt Lucas and Hugh Bonneville among actors calling for law on AI voice cloning</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4gv5gepxnyo#0</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:32:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T05:11:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4gv5gepxnyo--58e9b6058619.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4gv5gepxnyo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The performers are asking the government to give every person in the UK a legal right to own their voice.</summary></entry><entry><title>Time is running out for cyber security, warn top tech firms</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyz11475l1o#0</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:32:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T19:44:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyz11475l1o--ca07bdfa4c8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyz11475l1o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The letter warns cyber-attacks which use AI will become more sophisticated in a matter of months.</summary></entry><entry><title>Reform of all social media should come with Meta changes, UN says</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c17j00lnn41o#0</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:32:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T19:31:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c17j00lnn41o--4aea022a8c10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c17j00lnn41o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">California's attorney general is now looking at TikTok and YouTube to enact teen safety features.</summary></entry><entry><title>What the Meta settlement means for the UK, and other questions after the deal</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cg49q4xydq0o#0</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:32:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T13:24:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cg49q4xydq0o--1a614c31bf00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cg49q4xydq0o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Other social media firms are yet to respond, while the debate from campaigners is far from over.</summary></entry><entry><title>Unexpected chat between OpenAI agents led to Hugging Face hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj9xj89dk40o#0</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:32:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T22:03:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj9xj89dk40o--9600a6045ea5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj9xj89dk40o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">OpenAI's cyber agents banded together to perform a hack during a security test.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia revenue doubles on continued AI demand</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce871n7lyvlo#0</id><updated>2026-08-31T21:32:06Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T21:49:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce871n7lyvlo--bb58c28efbc6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce871n7lyvlo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Chipmaker's $96bn quarter beat forecasts as demand for AI hardware continues to accelerate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Meta to pay up to $18bn to settle claims its platforms harm children</title><id>https://www.